      "content": " Input: [[1, 3], [2, 6], [8, 10], [15, 18]] Output: [[1, 6], [8, 10], [15, 18]]\n\n```python\nfrom typing import List, Tuple\n\ndef merge_intervals(intervals: List[Tuple[int, int]]) -> List[Tuple[int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Merge overlapping or touching intervals and return sorted merged intervals.\n    \n    Args:\n        intervals: List of [start, end] integer pairs\n        \n    Returns:\n        List of merged [start, end] pairs, sorted by start value\n    \"\"\"\n    if not intervals:\n        return []\n    \n    # Sort intervals by start time\n    sorted_intervals = sorted(intervals)\n    merged = [list(sorted_intervals[0])]\n    \n    for start, end in sorted_intervals[1:]:\n        # If current interval overlaps or touches the last merged interval\n        if start <= merged[-1][1]:\n            # Merge by updating the end time\n            merged[-1][1] = max(merged[-1][1], end)\n        else:\n            # Add new interval\n            merged.append([start, end])\n    \n    return [tuple(interval) for interval in merged]\n```",
